scripts (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Block arms in a `match` expression (`=> { ...; value }`); a map literal arm is
    written `({ ... })` (breaking syntax).
  * New `process.exit_with_message`, `result.ignore_error`, `SCRIPTS-LINT-0013`
    and `SCRIPTS-LINT-0014` with `check --fix`, integer/float math methods,
    `string.find_all_regex`, `encoding.url_encode`/`url_decode`,
    `list<T>.chunked`, and the intrinsic `csv` module.
  * Removed `process.run_shell` (rejected statically with `SCRIPTS-TYPE-0068`).
  * .NET SDK 10.0.404 (runtime and Native AOT ILCompiler 10.0.15) with the
    November 2026 .NET runtime security fixes.
  * A `SIGINT` or `SIGHUP` ignored at startup stays ignored (POSIX convention);
    fixed a lost wake-up that could hang `parallel.run_all`.

 -- Younes BENMOUSSA <younes.benmoussa@pm.me>  Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:22:20 +0000

scripts (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Make the release gate portable on GitHub Actions: CPU-count-aware parallel
    bound and a descriptor probe above stdio. No language change.

 -- Younes BENMOUSSA <younes.benmoussa@pm.me>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:06:46 +0000

scripts (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix a closed standard input when the .NET runtime owns descriptor 0: treat
    it as an absent stream, not as a script (GitHub Actions, 251 regression).

 -- Younes BENMOUSSA <younes.benmoussa@pm.me>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:57:27 +0000

scripts (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First public release of Scripts 0.1.0.
    - the `scripts` command, `.scs` source files and `SCRIPTS-*` error codes;
    - static checker, `run`, `check`, `explain`, `fmt --check` and
      `describe --format json`, with `--errors-json` and `--json-out`;
    - frozen standard library (filesystem, processes, environment) with typed
      errors and bounded-concurrency helpers, including process.set_umask,
      filesystem.make_hard_link, filesystem.get_file_system_status,
      integer.absolute and float.absolute;
    - Native AOT interpreter binary, no .NET runtime dependency;
    - vendored Core subset (Results, Serialization.Values, Concurrency) under
      LGPL-3.0-or-later; the language itself is GPL-3.0-or-later.

 -- Younes BENMOUSSA <younes.benmoussa@pm.me>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
